                "caption": "Figure 1:An overview ofJ-Zero, in which the Challenger, Solver, and Judge are jointly updated\nthrough iterative self-play.Top and Middle:In the Challenger and Solver training phases, the two policies are trained adversarially under the frozen Judge. The Challenger generates tasks on which the Solver scores poorly, and the Solver learns to recover high scores on those tasks.Bottom:In the Judge training phase, the Judge is updated on two types of in-loop preference pairs, role asymmetry (𝒟role\\mathcal{D}_{\\mathrm{role}}) and subtask amplification (𝒟amp\\mathcal{D}_{\\mathrm{amp}}), so that its evaluation ability rises in step with the two policies it supervises.",
